  "body": "This PR adds a Sodick wire EDM machine file, \"Sodick ALC400G\" (kind `wire_edm`), to the built-in library.\n\nWhat changed:\n- New file `assets/machines/sodick-alc400g.mch`, registered in `posting::MACHINES`.\n- It states X 400 mm, Y 300 mm, U 150 mm, V 150 mm of travel and `edm.max_taper_deg` 25.\n- Each travel is stated centred on zero. The sources give the length, not the machine origin.\n- The numbers with no public source are left out: guide heights, AWT, wire diameters, conditions and codes. The app refuses a cut by name until the user adds a condition from their own control.\n- The Sodick post is offered for the file, like for every wire machine. The ALC400G is not confirmed to use the Mark 21 control that the post was written from. The post still says \"not verified\" in each program.\n- Decision record: `docs/decisions/1501-sodick-alc400g.md`.\n\nRework after the review:\n- Taper source: the figure of 25 degrees stays. The Sodick Thailand page https://www.sodick.co.th/EN/EDW.php lists the ALC400G taper angle as +-25 deg at work height 130 mm. The 30 deg on that page belongs to the ALC800GH and ALN800GH, not to the ALC400G. The sodick.eu page gives the travels only. It states no taper for this model.\n- Taper limit: the taper figure is data only. The file states no guide heights, so the post refuses a tapered cut by name. The Sodick post (`sodick-wire.cps`) writes a vertical 2-axis cut only, so it refuses every taper. The schema gap is tracked in #1800. This PR changes no schema, no post code and no posted G-code.\n- The machine file now carries a `general.description` with the sources and this limit.\n\n- Second rework: the ribbon has a Wire EDM mode row (`MACHINE_MODES`). The Machine tip text in `tips_match_the_imgui_table` lists it. The clippy `err_expect` finding is fixed.\nSources (public, Sodick):\n- https://www.sodick.co.th/EN/EDW.php (taper, travels)\n- https://sodick.eu/products/wire-edm (travels)\n- Sodick ALC series brochure, text copy: https://www.scribd.com/document/479890863/Sodick-ALC-series-wire-cut-EDM-machines\n\nTests (`crates/app/tests/sodick_alc400g.rs`): `the_machine_file_states_only_the_published_figures`, `the_library_lists_it_and_offers_the_sodick_post`, `the_shipped_file_refuses_a_cut_until_the_user_states_a_condition`, `a_punch_posts_through_the_sodick_post_on_it`, and the new `a_tapered_punch_is_refused_at_post_while_the_file_states_no_guide_heights`. All 5 pass. Also updated the pinned list in `crates/app/tests/machine.rs`.\n\nNot exercised: the quick gate after the rework (only the `sodick_alc400g` suite ran). Posted output was not run on a Sodick control. No UI check.\n\nChangelog: Added the Sodick ALC400G wire EDM machine file (#1501, travels and taper from Sodick's published specifications)\nEffort: medium\n\nRefs #1800\nFixes #1501\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
